[Round 6/8 | Implementer | 233.6s | 0/400k] I found the concrete lost-signal window: the lane publication tail is advanced before the token CAS, so a consumer can refresh that tail, then clear an already-set lane bit after the producer claims the token; the tail does not change and the signal is lost. I’m moving the tail publication to immediately after the successful authoritative token CAS, then retaining the required pre/post-clear tail checks. This makes the tail a true publication witness instead of a preparation witness.

