[Round 6/8 | Implementer | 599.7s | 0/400k] The longer run exposed that the remaining hot cost is mostly synchronization traffic: every successful enqueue performs an active-word RMW even when its lane is already signaled, and every dequeue resets metadata that the next producer overwrites before publication. I’m reducing those redundant atomics while relying on the newly-correct tail recheck to preserve signal safety; the authoritative token CAS and token validation remain unchanged.

