[Round 6/8 | Implementer | 1081.0s | 0/400k] The shared negative-scan cache is now global and invalidated before every token release, so only one producer performs an authoritative no-free scan per release epoch; successful claims still require the token CAS, and no bitmap/count is used as correctness state. This brought the three long samples to 1.23M, 1.64M, and 2.09M ops/s locally (median just above the 1,598,401 target), while all correctness tests remain green. I’m stress-checking the cache/hint interaction and finalizing the artifact.

