[Round 6/8 | Implementer | 2313.0s | 0/400k] The long-run native-target samples are being throttled to ~1.1M despite short bursts above 2M, so compiler flags alone cannot satisfy the gate. I found a safe M5-specific optimization that preserves the original race repair: the tail-record recheck is only needed after a bounded repair has moved a lane cursor; it is currently repeated on every ordinary refresh. I’m adding a preallocated per-lane “repair recheck pending” bit so ordinary active-lane/dequeued-lane refreshes skip that dead work while repaired lanes still perform the exact validation.

